<title>USA: Roller Bearing Co to sell $100 mln in junk bonds.</title>
<headline>Roller Bearing Co to sell $100 mln in junk bonds.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Roller Bearing Company of America, plans to sell $100 million in 10-year senior subordinated debt in a 144a private placement in the next several weeks, market sources said.</p>
<p>Proceeds from the deal will be used to pay shareholders of the privately held company a special dividend, the sources said.</p>
<p>The company makes precision non-automotive roller ball and plain bearings.</p>
<p>Credit Suisse First Boston will be the sole manager of the transaction.</p>
<p>The securities will be non-callable for five years.</p>
<p>-Douglas Brown, 212-859-1662</p>
